.el .ds Aq '
.TH "skillastic monitor" 1  "skillastic monitor " 
.SH NAME
skillastic monitor \- Manage the multi\-repo daemon supervisor (used by the systemd unit `enroll` installs; rarely invoked directly)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskillastic monitor\fR [\fB\-\-system\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the multi\-repo daemon supervisor (used by the systemd unit `enroll` installs; rarely invoked directly)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-system\fR
Operate on the system\-wide registry instead of the per\-user one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
skillastic monitor\-add(1)
Register a project for monitoring (defaults to the current directory)
.TP
skillastic monitor\-remove(1)
Unregister a project (defaults to the current directory)
.TP
skillastic monitor\-list(1)
Show all registered projects and whether their daemon is running
.TP
skillastic monitor\-enable(1)
Enable monitoring for a project (defaults to the current directory)
.TP
skillastic monitor\-disable(1)
Disable monitoring for a project (defaults to the current directory)
.TP
skillastic monitor\-resume(1)
Start daemons for all enabled, not\-running projects
.TP
skillastic monitor\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
